Selected object timelines, relative to final equipment signal
- Trial 2 Actor.HasPerk: other stack 1486086 acquired at 61.554, before Q at 61.606, and released at 84.687. More contenders acquired the same token. Stack 1486073 released at 109.455, acquired again at 132.474, and stack 1486096 acquired at 132.645. The final stack took the token at 155.856 after 1486096 released it at 155.816. HasPerk dispatch took 0.003 ms and did not miss its return lock.
- Trial 3 Form.HasKeyword: stack 1486824 released the target at 135.838, 0.127 ms after the stock pass ended at 135.711. The final stack acquired at 158.987, in the next stock pass. Trial 4 shows the analogous pattern with the previous stock pass ending at 134.056, release at 134.182 and acquisition at 158.023. These times place both slow calls before dispatch and show the pattern in both arms.
- Trial 8: stack 1489612 was queued 347.255 ms before entering, and entered 0.005 ms after the previous HeelsFixCorrectEffect.OnObjectUnequipped stack 1489590 finished. No advance occurred anywhere in trial 8. Trial 7's tail was the preceding unequip handler, entered 0.008 ms after the previous handler of the same class finished, and spent 237.629 ms after Actor.HasSpell returned with ten return lock misses.

