- OFF 1 / ON 2: tail +52.482 ms, sum of tail native queue waits +50.069 ms. Actor.HasPerk alone increased from 24.818 to 94.251 ms while Actor.IsSneaking decreased from 47.307 to 23.611 ms.
- OFF 4 / ON 3: tail +1.153 ms, sum of tail native queue waits +0.836 ms. The slow Form.HasKeyword wait is present in both modes.
- OFF 6 / ON 5: tail -23.016 ms, sum of tail native queue waits -21.103 ms. The second NetImmerse.HasNode wait went from 46.168 to 21.643 ms.

The median tail increased in this sample. The largest positive pair difference is in the interval before entering native frames on the final handler. Neither that long wait nor the similar HasKeyword waits overlap an advanced pass. This supports contention and waiting for the stock suspended-stack phase as the observed source of these delays. The capture does not isolate indirect scheduling effects from advances earlier in the workload.
